<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Violencia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a>–<a href="/years/1958">1958</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Violencia was a civil conflict in Colombia between supporters of the Liberal and Conservative parties, usually dated from 1948 to 1958. Sparked by the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jorge-eliecer-gaitan">Jorge Eliécer Gaitán</a>, it spread through the countryside in massacres, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war and police terror, killing around 200,000 people. It ended with the power-sharing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-front-czechoslovakia">National Front</a>, but some of its armed bands later formed the core of leftist guerrillas such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolutionary-armed-forces-of-colombia">FARC</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-violencia.jpg" alt="La Violencia" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Pradilla Holguin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bogotazo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
